# ── Build output ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
bin/
tmp/
temp/
dist/
build/
*.exe
*.exe~

# ── Test & coverage ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.test
*.out
coverage.txt
coverage.html

# ── Go workspace ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
go.work
go.work.sum

# ── Task / tooling cache ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.task/
.devbox/
.venv/

# ── IDE / editor ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store

# Claude Code worktrees
.claude/worktrees/

# ── docc build output ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
output/

# ── Reference material (real client documents, never committed) ──────────────
# Drafting against real documents happens in the profile pack repository now.
# The entry stays as a backstop: a stray render here must never reach history.
assets/

# ── A local profile binding ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The firm's schemas and themes live in their own private pack repository. A
# `docc profile use` here writes a binding and lockfile for local drafting;
# that is one developer's convenience, not this repository's configuration.
.docc/

# ── Local secrets and machine-specific config ────────────────────────────────
# .env carries credentials for the MCP servers this repo is developed against;
# .mcp.json names them and is per-machine. Neither belongs in the history, and
# both sat untracked-but-not-ignored, one `git add -A` away from being pushed.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.mcp.json
